# Next.js 16 & React

- House rules, Project facts, and conventions live in `AGENTS.md`; library versions and docs in `docs/agent/stack.md`.
- Next.js 16 changed APIs: read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing Next code.
- Components under `src/app/` are RSC by default; mark `"use client"` only for hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers.
- Route files stay thin and compose a feature from `src/features/<feature>/`.
- Use path aliases: `@/`, `@app/`, `@components/`, `@features/`, `@lib/`.
- Use shadcn/ui (new-york) primitives from `src/components/ui/` and CVA for variants.
